# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Vreteno onto standard cells. The build fills in the words between
# the at signs: the sources the document build emitted, the top
# module, the timing library of the technology, the period the
# technology mapper aims at, and where the netlist and the cell count
# are to be written.
#
# Every line here is a step a reader can follow, and the order is the
# one the OpenROAD flow scripts use. It is worth keeping that order:
# the last six lines are what turns a netlist into something a layout
# can be made of, and getting them in the wrong sequence costs cells
# that nothing needs.

read_verilog @SOURCES@
hierarchy -check -top @TOP@

# The generic synthesis: elaborate, infer the memories and the
# arithmetic, map to generic gates, and optimise. The design is
# flattened because the core is one module already and its submodules
# are separate designs.
synth -top @TOP@ -flatten
opt -purge

# The technology: registers first, since a register can only be mapped
# to a cell that exists, and then the combinational logic, where ABC
# is told the period so that it knows which paths are worth the area.
dfflibmap -liberty @LIBERTY@
abc -liberty @LIBERTY@ -D @PERIOD_PS@

# What is left of the abstractions. Undefined bits become zero and
# every bus becomes its bits, because a netlist of cells has no such
# thing as a vector; then what nothing reads goes. Constants become
# the two cells that drive them, which the mapper will not use because
# the library marks them `dont_use`, and a port wired straight through
# to another gets a buffer, because a layout has no such thing as a
# wire with no driver.
#
# The order of these six is the one the OpenROAD flow scripts use, and
# it is not decoration: buffering before the buses are split puts a
# buffer on every bit of every bus, which here was three thousand
# eight hundred cells that nothing needed.
setundef -zero
splitnets
opt_clean -purge
hilomap -hicell LOGIC1_X1 Z -locell LOGIC0_X1 Z -singleton
insbuf -buf BUF_X1 A Z

tee -o @STATS@ stat -liberty @LIBERTY@
write_verilog -noattr @NETLIST@
